## Inputs

- `keywords.txt`: one keyword per line (what each site is searched for)
- `settings.json`: pages per keyword, pauses, output format/columns, site-specific blocks

## Outputs

- `output/{{slug}}_<date>.xlsx`: one file per run (never overwritten; a second run the same day gets a time suffix)
- `output/latest.xlsx`: always the most recent run
- Copy of every file: `{{outputs_dir}}`
- History (what is "new"): `data/leads.db` (**never delete**)
- Sheets: *New this run*, *All leads*, *Run history*, *Problems* (only when something failed)

## Run and test

```bash
.venv/bin/python run.py --list                                   # sites + keywords
.venv/bin/python run.py --site <site> --keyword "<kw>" --dry-run --headed   # test one
.venv/bin/python run.py                                          # the real run
```
Non-technical use: double-click `Run Automation.command` (Mac) / `Run Automation.bat` (Windows).
Logins: `.venv/bin/python run.py --login <site>`. Schedule: `.venv/bin/python tools/schedule_daily.py --time 09:00`.

